Subject: [PATCH] vkr: write each queue submission into vmlab-hv's GPU trace (diagnostics)

Diagnostics only; not applied by build/hv.py, which takes
patches/virglrenderer/*.patch and not this directory. Applies on 1.3.0
after 0001 to 0003. Card #237, guest/win3d/docs/tearing.md.

With VMLAB_HV_GPU_TRACE=<dir> in its environment (vmlab-hv's own trace
switch, which the render server inherits), each render worker writes
<dir>/gpu-trace-<pid>.txt in the format of vmlab-hv's trace
(hv/crates/vmlab-hv-display/src/trace.rs): one line per event, the time
on CLOCK_MONOTONIC first.

- vk_submit: every vkQueueSubmit and vkQueueSubmit2, at the time the ring
  thread hands it to the host driver, with the context id and name, the
  queue, the fence, each batch's wait and signal semaphores (with timeline
  values) and command buffers, and the virgl resources those command
  buffers use: w for an attachment, a copy, blit, resolve or clear
  destination, r for a copy source, d through a bound or pushed
  descriptor, b named by a barrier. The resources are found through the
  objects the context made: memory imported from a resource or exported
  as one, images and buffers bound to it, views, framebuffers and
  descriptor set slots.
- vk_done: when an empty submission with a fence of the trace, made on the
  same queue right after the traced one, signals. The host GPU has
  finished the traced submission's work by then.

Off, it costs one branch per hooked command.
---
